<title>GERMANY: Morgan Stanley ups share outlook for German banks. [CORRECTED 10:28 GMT]</title>
<headline>Morgan Stanley ups share outlook for German banks. [CORRECTED 10:28 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morgan Stanley said on Friday it had raised its forecast for the development of the share prices of Germany's top three commercial banks Deutsche Bank AG, Dresdner Bank AG and Commerzbank AG by 10 percent each.  </p>
<p>Banking analyst Olaf Conrad said he had increased his share price target for Deutsche to 87 marks, for Dresdner to 55 (corrects from 46) marks and for Commerzbank to 46 (corrects from 55) marks.</p>
<p>-Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
